  "details": "Sortedby groups friends properly, hardcoded groupings break it:\n\nThe \"Recently Seen\" tab sorted by \"Last Visited\" used to be a very good timeline to contextualize recent activity and new friends invites, since the last update friends and strangers are now no longer interlaced/properly sorted but in complete seperate groupings. [\"Friends\", \"Other Users\"]\n\nThe \"All Friends\" list does the same, if I want to search for my friend \"K\", I have to check\n\nK in [\"None\", \" Active on another platform\", \"Discord\", \"Offline\"]\n\nSuggested fix: Toggle groupings off button\n\nAlternative Suggested fix: Move hardcoded groupings to their own sortedby setting. eg \"platform\"or \"isFriend\" for \"All Friends\" and \"Recently Seen\" respectively. \n\nHave a nice day.\n\nBullet",
